  <file source-language="en" target-language="en" datatype="plaintext" original="tui">
    <header>
      <note>Every string the terminal administration shows, and the page of the loopback interface the browser is answered with once it brought the authorization response back. ICU message format: {issuer} is the issuer of the tenant, {profile} the name the profile of the instance was kept under, {administrator} the name of who signed in, {acr} the class of their authentication, {url} the address of the authorization endpoint, {redirect_uri} the redirect URI of the client, {reason} why the sign-in or a read of the administration API failed, {minutes} and {time} how long the access token is worth and until when, {time} also when a session was authenticated, {days} a number of days, {count} a number of rows, {client} the identifier of a client, {username} the username the administrator typed or the API answered, {kind} and {name} the kind and the name of a credential, {address} the address a session was last seen from, {since} the start of the window the statistics count over. value.more is a printf pattern, %d being how many items were left out. A string named refusal.&lt;error&gt; is what the screen says to do when the provider refuses a sign-in with that error, api.refusal.&lt;error&gt; when the administration API refuses a request with it, act.&lt;name&gt; how the screen names an act of the journal, and key.status.&lt;state&gt; how it names the state of a signing key.</note>
    </header>
